  "result": "Defaults in `default_map` now reach subcommands, and the full test suite passes.\n\n**Cause:** in `Context.__init__` (`src/click/core.py`), a child context inherited its parent's whole `default_map`. So for `{\"foo\": {\"name\": \"bar\"}}` the subcommand `foo` saw the group-level dict and never found `name`.\n\n**Fix:** the child now takes `parent.default_map.get(info_name)`, which is the entry for the subcommand's own name. It's a one-line change.\n\n**Test:** I added `test_default_map_subcommand` in `tests/test_defaults.py`. I did not first confirm that it fails without the fix.\n\nWhile adding the test I accidentally cut two lines from the end of `test_flag_default_map`, which made the new test fail. I restored those lines and re-ran the suite.\n\nI didn't touch `CHANGES.md` or `docs/`, which `CLAUDE.md` asks for on user-visible changes. I held off because I'm not sure this counts as one, so say if you want entries added.",
